	I just got a hold of Nethack 3.0 (pl 6) sources just a bit ago (thanks
to some helpful people participating in the newsgroup) and have ported them
to my 286 PC at home.  Reading through the material on porting, I've gotten
the impression that perhaps the development team, and everyone else for that
matter, have essentially "given up" on clean Turbo C ports.  Full option
compiles are not practical because the overlay manager included only works
with Microsoft C.   Is there any future (at all?) for some sort of overlay
manager for Turbo C'ers?   I know that Borland did not provide any means 
for this in the language itself, but (and I caution that I'm far from being
the software/assembler engineering genius that some people apparenty are!)
coudln't some overlay manager be created to fit the other language's
specifications?

